# The build context, not the image: the Dockerfile copies only `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `src`
# and `config`, so nothing below lands in a layer today. The context transfer itself is the
# exposure the moment the builder is not local -- buildx against a remote builder, a shared
# BuildKit daemon, kaniko, a hosted CI build -- and `.env` holds the real database password and
# the long-lived Google refresh token. The credential shapes are the ones `.gitignore` names.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
application_default_credentials.json

.git/
.venv/
.planning/
.claude/
.gsd/
tests/
migrations/
k8s/

__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
